asset.differentiation_notes:
1. Mechanism precision: first drug targeting thalamocortical oscillatory circuit;
   propranolol/primidone are non-specific.
2. Tolerability: Phase 2 3% discontinuation vs. 15-20% for propranolol/primidone;
   no sedation, no sexual dysfunction, no cognitive effects.
3. Untreated market: 75% of moderate-severe ET patients are untreated; better
   tolerability is the key to unlocking this population.
4. Responder profile: 50% tremor reduction in 65% of patients (Phase 2);
   much higher response rate than historical propranolol data.
5. QD/BID dosing (oral); convenient for elderly population (median ET age: 65+).
